  "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{\u2032}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=7$ and $v(x)=2{x}^{2}-5x-3,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n{u}^{\u2032}(x)=0,\\,{v}^{\u2032}(x)=4x-5.\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x){v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0)\\cdot (2{x}^{2}-5x-3)-7\\cdot (4x-5)}{{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7\\cdot (4x-5)}{{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(5-4x)}{{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
